 ## Background
-WISE is based on the shear-warp factorization of the viewing transformation, originally presented by Lacroute in 1994 [S1, book]. The method was developed to accelerate visibility tests in large-scale isosurface extraction, where the cost of perspective projection for every vertex of meta-cells and triangles is prohibitive [S1, book]. It is used in real-time ray-tracing and volume rendering applications, particularly in medical imaging, where interactive isosurface control is required [S1, book].
